{"ts": 0.087881, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97m3.2 — reading: cat, less\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[92mcat\u001b[0m prints the entire file at once.\r\n  \u001b[92mcat hello.txt\u001b[0m                \u001b[90m# probably empty\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mcat ../poem.txt\u001b[0m        \u001b[90m# the tutor's poem, one folder up\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nFor a long file, \u001b[92mcat\u001b[0m floods the screen. Use \u001b[92mless\u001b[0m\r\nto page through it:\r\n  \u001b[92mless ../numbers.txt\u001b[0m    \u001b[90m# 50 lines — more than one screen\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nInside \u001b[92mless\u001b[0m, the screen takes over. Press \u001b[95mSpace\u001b[0m\r\nor \u001b[95mf\u001b[0m to page down, \u001b[95mb\u001b[0m to page back, and\r\n\u001b[95mq\u001b[0m to exit. (More on full-screen programs in Stage 5.)\r\n\r\n\u001b[91mImportant:\u001b[0m when \u001b[92mless\u001b[0m takes over, the prompt is\r\ngone. You're inside a program. \u001b[95mq\u001b[0m returns you to the shell.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Try both, then \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 778}
{"ts": 0.088281, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 251}
